PR description to grade:

### What is this change?

Adds a `PATCH /orders/{id}/status` endpoint that lets Support-role agents update an order's status and records when the change was made. This is for customer support agents who currently request these updates from logistics by email.

### Type of change?

- New feature (non-breaking change which adds functionality)

### Why?

Customer support currently sends roughly 400 order status updates per week to the logistics team over email. Each hand-off takes 20–40 minutes and can be lost between inboxes. Letting agents with the Support role set an order to "Shipped" directly removes most of the manual work and reduces the time before customers see the updated status from hours to minutes.

### How?

- Adds the `UpdateOrderStatusRequest` DTO with a required `Status` field validated against `Pending|Shipped|Delivered|Cancelled`.
- Adds `UpdateStatusAsync` to `OrderService`, which finds the order, sets `order.Status` and `order.StatusUpdatedAt` to `DateTime.UtcNow`, persists the change, and returns `true` or `false` for found or not found.
- Adds the `PATCH /orders/{id}/status` endpoint in `OrdersController`, restricted to the `Support` role, returning `204 NoContent` on success or `404 NotFound` when the order does not exist.
- Adds a SQL migration that adds a nullable `StatusUpdatedAt datetime2` column to the `Orders` table.
- Adds a unit test in `OrdersControllerTests` covering the existing-order success case for `UpdateStatus`.

### Requires Manual Database Migration?

Yes.

```sql
ALTER TABLE Orders ADD StatusUpdatedAt datetime2 NULL;
GO
```

### Anything Else?

The new endpoint is additive and does not affect existing order endpoints. `StatusUpdatedAt` is nullable, so existing orders can still be updated without a pre-existing timestamp. Only users in the Support role can call the new endpoint.

Rubric criterion:

The "Why?" field explains the business reason stated in the User Story (support handling ~400 manual status updates per week, 20-40 minute hand-offs, hours-to-minutes delay), not a restatement of the code change.


